## 5. MATHEMATICAL MODEL & SUCCESS CRITERIA

### 5.1 Separation Efficiency Definition

The primary metric is

$$\eta = \frac{m_{\text{ice,collected}}}{m_{\text{ice,initial}}} \times 100\%.$$

Phase 1 target: $\eta \geq 20\%$ with ice purity $P \geq 60\%$.

### 5.2 Acoustic Attenuation Validation

The go/no‑go criterion is:
- $\alpha < 10$ dB/mm (i.e., <20 dB total over 2 mm) → **Go** for 40 kHz.
- $\alpha$ 10–20 dB/mm → **Caution**, consider frequency reduction.
- $\alpha > 20$ dB/mm → **No‑go**, shift to 25 kHz.

### 5.3 Triboelectric Charge Verification

Phase 1 Test B3 must demonstrate a total collected charge >10 nC from the ice‑regolith mixture at 100 K. This threshold is above the electrometer noise floor and confirms that tribocharging is active.

### 5.4 Integrated Performance

Cascaded efficiency is predicted as:
$$\eta_{\text{total}} = \eta_{\text{fluid}} \cdot \eta_{\text{strat}} \cdot \eta_{\text{col}} \approx 0.8 \times 0.4 \times 0.75 \approx 24\%.$$

If any stage underperforms, the bottleneck will be identified through the phased test protocol.

