## 7. PHASE 1 TESTING & VALIDATION PROTOCOL

### 7.1 Subsystem Verification (Tests A1–A4)

**A1 – Vibration Fluidization @ 100 K**: Confirm Faraday fluidization of dry simulant at 0.7 g.  
**A2 – Acoustic Field & Attenuation**: Map pressure field and measure $\alpha$ over 2 mm. Decision gate for frequency.  
**A3 – Electrostatic Field**: Verify quadrupole symmetry at 2 kV.  
**A4 – Thermal Stability**: Demonstrate 100 K ± 0.5 K during combined operation.

### 7.2 Component Testing (Tests B1–B4)

**B1 – Vibration‑Only Liberation**: Quantify ice displacement without acoustics.  
**B2 – Vibration + Acoustics**: Observe ice stratification at top/bottom nodes; confirm Φ > 0.  
**B3 – Vibration + Electrostatics**: Measure tribocharge collected at 100 K (first experimental data point).  
**B4 – Full Hybrid**: Run complete sequence and measure separation efficiency and purity.

### 7.3 Parameter Optimisation (Tests C1–C3)

Sweeps of phase timing, acoustic frequency (20–60 kHz), and temperature (80–120 K) to identify optimum operating conditions.

### 7.4 Endurance & Reliability (Tests D1–D2)

24‑hour continuous operation and 1000 on/off cycles to identify failure modes, vacuum degradation, and regolith compaction.

**Go/No‑Go Decision Flow (summarised)**
- A2 attenuation >20 dB/mm → shift to 25 kHz.
- B3 charge <10 nC → tribocharging insufficient; consider surface treatments.
- B4 efficiency <10 % → fundamental bottleneck; re‑evaluate concept.

